      "text": "On 6 March 2024, the ALP protocol on BNB Chain was exploited for approximately $10,000. The attack leveraged an externally callable privileged function, enabling unauthorized withdrawals of protocol assets. A privileged internal function was incorrectly exposed as external, allowing any address to trigger asset transfers intended only for protocol operations. Insufficient access control permitted an attacker to drain funds."
